--text-primary);">init_db(filename, cmd-&gt;cols, cmd-&gt;col_count)</code>=
).</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Why?</strong></p>
<ol style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: v=
ar(--text-primary);">Atomicity:</strong> File creation and initialization s=
hould happen together. If <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--b=
g-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padd=
ing: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">init_=
db</code> creates a file with an empty header, and the system crashes befor=
e the caller overwrites it with real columns, you are left with a corrupt, =
uninitialized database file that looks valid.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: v=
ar(--text-primary);">Encapsulation:</strong> The storage module (<code clas=
s=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--b=
order-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-=
sm); color: var(--text-primary);">storage.c</code>) should be the only laye=
r that knows about the <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-r=
aised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding=
: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">Header</=
code> struct. If you force the caller (<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"backgr=
ound: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radi=
us: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-pri=
mary);">executor.c</code>) to overwrite the header manually, you are leakin=
g storage implementation details into the execution layer.</li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">I can have <code class=
=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--bo=
rder-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-s=
m); color: var(--text-primary);">writer-append</code> update <code class=3D=
"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--borde=
r-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm);=
 color: var(--text-primary);">init_db</code> to take the column list and in=
