<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">What was changed:</h3>
<ol style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"bac=
kground: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-r=
adius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-=
primary);">execute_insert</code>:</strong></p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It now generates a filename based on the ta=
ble name (e.g. <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); =
border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5p=
x; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">users.db</code>)=
.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It calls your <code class=3D"mono" style=3D=
"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); bord=
er-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--t=
ext-primary);">init_db(filename, cmd-&gt;cols, cmd-&gt;col_count)</code> to=
 ensure the file and header exist.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It populates a <code class=3D"mono" style=
=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); b=
order-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(=
--text-primary);">Record</code> struct with the values from the command.</l=
i>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It opens the file and calls your <code clas=
s=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--b=
order-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-=
sm); color: var(--text-primary);">append_record(f, &amp;new_record)</code>.=
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"bac=
kground: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-r=
adius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-=
primary);">execute_select</code>:</strong></p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It opens the table file in read mode.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It reads the <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"=
background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); borde=
r-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--te=
xt-primary);">Header</code> to find out how many columns to print and what =
their names are.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It loops from <code class=3D"mono" style=3D=
"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); bord=
er-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--t=
ext-primary);">0</code> to <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--=
bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; pad=
ding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">head=
er.row_count</code> and calls your <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background=
: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: =
4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary=
);">read_record(f, i, &amp;current_record)</code>.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It neatly formats and prints every column o=
f every record that isn't marked as deleted.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">The executor has trans=
itioned from returning mock strings to actually saving data to your disk ma=
nager. You should be able to compile this and test a basic <code class=3D"m=
ono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-=
subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); c=
