file on your disk.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Here is the difference=
 between what we have now and what a Page/Buffer Pool architecture does:</p=
>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">What we have now (Direct I/O):</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">When you type <code cl=
ass=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(-=
-border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--tex=
t-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">SELECT * FROM cars</code>, <code class=
=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--bo=
rder-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-s=
m); color: var(--text-primary);">executor.c</code> opens the file, uses <co=
de class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid =
var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(=
--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">fseek</code> to jump to a row on t=
he hard drive, and uses <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-=
raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; paddin=
g: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">fread</=
code> to pull that single row straight from the disk to the terminal.
If you type that query 100 times, the database hits the hard drive 100 time=
s. Hard drives are extremely slow.</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">What Page Architecture does (Cached I/O):</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Your tables are still =
saved as <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border=
: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; fon=
t-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">.db</code> files on yo=
ur disk. But the <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised)=
; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px =
5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">.db</code> fil=
e is now chopped up into 4KB chunks called <strong style=3D"font-weight: 60=
0; color: var(--text-primary);">Pages</strong>.</p>
<ol style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">When you type <code class=3D"mono" style=3D=
"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); bord=
er-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--t=
ext-primary);">SELECT * FROM cars</code>, the Buffer Pool Manager checks if=
 Page 1 is in RAM.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">If it's not, it reads the 4KB chunk from th=
e disk <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">once=
</strong> and keeps it in a RAM array (the Buffer Pool).</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It finds your record inside that 4KB chunk =
in RAM and returns it.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">If you run the query again, it reads from t=
he RAM copy instantly. Zero disk hits.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">If you <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"backgr=
ound: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radi=
us: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-pri=
mary);">UPDATE</code> a record, you update the copy in RAM. The Buffer Pool=
 Manager marks that page as "dirty" and eventually flushes the whole 4KB bl=
ock back to the hard drive to ensure it is saved permanently.</li>
</ol>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">In short:</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Disk is for permanent storage. RA=
M (the Buffer Pool) is for speed.</strong></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">You still write to dis=
k, you just read/write in 4096-byte blocks (Pages) instead of 1060-byte ind=
ividual <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border:=
 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font=
-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">Record</code> structs.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Would you like me to s=
how you what the C <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raise=
d); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1p=
x 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">struct</code=
> for a Slotted Page looks like, so you can see how records fit inside a 4K=
B block?</p></div><div class=3D"kp-turn__foot"><div class=3D"kp-actions"><b=
