<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">Phase 2: Page Architecture &amp; Indexing (C Engine)</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">The current flat-file =
<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px sol=
id var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: v=
ar(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">storage.c</code> will be replac=
ed by a Page-oriented design:</p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: v=
ar(--text-primary);">Slotted Pages (<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"backgroun=
d: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius:=
 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primar=
y);">page/</code>)</strong>: Instead of writing individual structs, the dis=
k manager will read/write fixed 4KB blocks. This fixes internal fragmentati=
on and allows variable-length strings.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: v=
ar(--text-primary);">Buffer Pool Manager (<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"bac=
kground: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-r=
adius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-=
primary);">buffer/</code>)</strong>: A caching layer that keeps frequently =
accessed 4KB pages in RAM (using an LRU eviction policy) to eliminate slow =
disk reads.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: v=
ar(--text-primary);">B+ Tree Index (<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"backgroun=
d: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius:=
 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primar=
y);">btree/</code>)</strong>: Instead of scanning every row to find a <code=
 class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid va=
r(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--=
text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">WHERE</code> match, a B+ Tree will m=
ap indexed values directly to their Page/Slot offsets.</li>
</ul>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">Phase 3: Networking &amp; Concurrency (Go Server)</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">The database will move=
 from a local CLI to a networked server.</p>
