=3D"font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-primary);"><p style=3D"margin: 0px 0=
px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">To build the <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600;=
 color: var(--text-primary);">Page</strong> layer, you are going to impleme=
nt a <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Slotte=
d Page Architecture</strong>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Instead of dealing wit=
h files directly, this layer only cares about managing a single 4096-byte (=
4KB) array in memory.</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">The Concept: How a Slotted Page Works</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Imagine a 4KB block of=
 memory.</p>
<ol style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">The <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; colo=
r: var(--text-primary);">Header</strong> goes at the very beginning (byte 0=
). It tracks the <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised)=
; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px =
5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">page_id</code>=
 and where the free space is.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">The <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; colo=
r: var(--text-primary);">Slot Array</strong> grows <em style=3D"font-style:=
 italic;">forwards</em> from the header. A slot just holds two integers: th=
e <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px s=
olid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size:=
 var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">offset</code> and <code class=
=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--bo=
rder-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-s=
m); color: var(--text-primary);">length</code> of a record.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">The <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; colo=
r: var(--text-primary);">Tuple Data</strong> (the actual strings/integers) =
is inserted at the very end of the 4KB block and grows <em style=3D"font-st=
yle: italic;">backwards</em>.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">The <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; colo=
r: var(--text-primary);">Free Space</strong> is the gap in the middle. When=
 the slot array and the tuple data meet, the page is full.</li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">This design is brillia=
nt because it easily handles variable-length data without wasting space.</p=
>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">The Structs (<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raise=
d); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1p=
x 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">cfiles/inclu=
de/page.h</code>)</h3>
<div class=3D"kepler-code-block"><div class=3D"kepler-code-block__toolbar">=
<span class=3D"kepler-code-block__lang mono">c</span><button type=3D"button=
