"8" rx=3D"2" ry=3D"2"></rect><path d=3D"M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2=
-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"></path></svg></button></div><pre class=3D"mono kepler=
-code-block__pre" style=3D"margin: 0px; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: var(-=
-text-sm); line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-primary); background: var(-=
-bg-base); overflow: auto; max-width: 100%;"><code>// 1. Setup a brand new =
4KB page in memory
void init_page(Page *page, uint32_t page_id);

// 2. Add a record.=20
// It calculates if there's enough room in the "free space" gap.
// If yes, it copies the data to the end, creates a slot, and returns the s=
lot_id.
// Returns -1 if the page is full.
int insert_tuple(Page *page, const char *record_data, uint16_t record_len);

// 3. Read a record using its slot_id.
// It looks up the slot array, finds the offset, and copies the data out.
bool get_tuple(Page *page, int slot_id, char *out_buffer);

// 4. Delete a record.
// Usually, you just set the slot's length to 0 (tombstone) or offset to 0.
// Later, you can write a "vacuum" function to defragment the page.
bool delete_tuple(Page *page, int slot_id);</code></pre></div>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">How this fits into your roadmap:</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Once you write these f=
