x; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">4095</code>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Now, let's look at <st=
rong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Step 2: The Bu=
ffer Pool Manager (<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raise=
d); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1p=
x 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">buffer/</cod=
e>)</strong>.</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">What is the Buffer Pool Manager?</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Your database is a fil=
e (or multiple files) on a hard drive, which we treat as a giant list of 4K=
B pages. But accessing the hard drive is incredibly slow.
The Buffer Pool Manager (BPM) solves this by allocating a chunk of RAM (the=
 "Buffer Pool") to cache pages.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">When your executor wan=
ts to read a page:</p>
<ol style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It asks the BPM for <code class=3D"mono" st=
yle=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle)=
; border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: v=
ar(--text-primary);">Page #3</code>.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">The BPM checks if <code class=3D"mono" styl=
e=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); =
border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var=
(--text-primary);">Page #3</code> is already in RAM. If so, it returns it i=
nstantly.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">If not, the BPM reads the 4KB chunk from th=
e <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px s=
olid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size:=
 var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">.db</code> file into a slot i=
n its RAM array (called a <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: var(--t=
ext-primary);">Frame</strong>), and returns it.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">If the RAM array is full, the BPM has to ki=
ck an old page out (using an eviction policy like <strong style=3D"font-wei=
ght: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">LRU - Least Recently Used</strong>) =
to make room. If the kicked-out page was modified (marked <strong style=3D"=
font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">dirty</strong>), the BPM wri=
tes it to disk first.</li>
</ol>
<hr style=3D"border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-right-width=
: medium; border-bottom-width: medium; border-left-width: medium; border-ri=
ght-style: none; border-bottom-style: none; border-left-style: none; border=
-right-color: currentcolor; border-bottom-color: currentcolor; border-left-=
color: currentcolor; border-image: none; margin: 12px 0px;">
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">Designing the Buffer Pool Manager</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">To build this, you nee=
d two new files: <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised)=
; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px =
5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">cfiles/include=
/buffer.h</code> and <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-rai=
sed); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: =
1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">cfiles/src=
/buffer/buffer.c</code>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">Here is the exact <cod=
e class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid v=
ar(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(-=
-text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">struct</code> design you should use=
 for <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1p=
x solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-si=
ze: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">buffer.h</code>:</p>
<div class=3D"kepler-code-block"><div class=3D"kepler-code-block__toolbar">=
<span class=3D"kepler-code-block__lang mono">c</span><button type=3D"button=
