t-primary);">cfiles/include/</code> and <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"backg=
round: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-rad=
ius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-pr=
imary);">buffer.c</code> in <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(-=
-bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; pa=
dding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">cfi=
les/src/buffer/</code>!</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">How the Buffer Pool Manager logic works:</h3>
<ol style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Eviction (LRU):</strong></p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">Look at <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"backg=
round: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-rad=
ius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-pr=
imary);">find_victim_frame</code>. It loops through the <code class=3D"mono=
" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-sub=
tle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); colo=
r: var(--text-primary);">frames</code> array (size 10) to find a frame with=
 <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px so=
lid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: =
var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">pin_count =3D=3D 0</code> (mea=
ning no thread is currently holding it).</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">If it finds an empty frame, it picks it imm=
ediately.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">Otherwise, it tracks <code class=3D"mono" s=
tyle=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle=
); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: =
var(--text-primary);">last_used</code> and evicts the one with the lowest t=
imestamp (Least Recently Used).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Fetching Pages:</strong></p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">Look at <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"backg=
round: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-rad=
ius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-pr=
imary);">fetch_page</code>. It first checks if the <code class=3D"mono" sty=
le=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);=
 border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: va=
r(--text-primary);">page_id</code> is already in memory (Cache Hit).</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">If it's a Cache Miss, it gets a victim fram=
e. If that victim was marked <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(=
--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; p=
adding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">is=
_dirty</code> (modified), it writes it out to disk permanently before overw=
riting it.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It calculates the disk offset simply as <co=
de class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid =
var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(=
--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">page_id * PAGE_SIZE (4096)</code>.=
 It uses <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border=
: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; fon=
t-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">fseek</code> and <code=
 class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid va=
r(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--=
text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">fread</code> to load that 4KB chunk =
from disk straight into the RAM frame.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Pinning:</strong></p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">When the executor asks for a page, <code cl=
ass=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(-=
-border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--tex=
t-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">fetch_page</code> sets <code class=3D"m=
ono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-=
subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); c=
olor: var(--text-primary);">pin_count =3D 1</code>. This locks the page in =
RAM so the eviction policy can't steal it while the executor is inserting a=
 tuple.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">When the executor is done, it MUST call <co=
de class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid =
var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(=
--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">unpin_page(pool, page_id, true/fal=
se)</code>. If the executor modified the data (like an <code class=3D"mono"=
 style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subt=
le); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color=
: var(--text-primary);">INSERT</code>), it passes <code class=3D"mono" styl=
e=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); =
border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var=
(--text-primary);">true</code> so the Buffer Pool knows it must be saved to=
 disk later.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">This Buffer Pool Manag=
er fully abstracts the hard drive away. The rest of the database (like your=
 upcoming B+ Tree) will just call <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background:=
 var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4=
px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary)=
;">fetch_page(pool, 3)</code> and magically get a 4KB memory pointer, compl=
etely unaware of whether it came from RAM or disk.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">The next step in your =
roadmap is <strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">=
Indexing (B+ Tree)</strong>. Let me know when you are ready to tackle it!</=
