-text-primary);">Transactions and Recovery (WAL)</strong> layer!</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">What I built:</h3>
<ol style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"bac=
kground: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-r=
adius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-=
primary);">wal.h</code> and <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(-=
-bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; pa=
dding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">wal=
.c</code> (Write-Ahead Logging)</strong></p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><strong style=3D"font-weight: 600; color: v=
ar(--text-primary);">The Rule of WAL</strong>: You <em style=3D"font-style:=
 italic;">must</em> write the change to the log file on disk <em style=3D"f=
ont-style: italic;">before</em> you are allowed to write the actual databas=
e page to disk. If the database crashes, the log survives.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: v=
ar(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px=
; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);"=
>LogRecord</code>: Tracks the <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var=
(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; =
padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">t=
xn_id</code>, what happened (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE), the <code class=3D"mo=
no" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-s=
ubtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); co=
lor: var(--text-primary);">page_id</code>/<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"bac=
kground: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-r=
adius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-=
primary);">slot_id</code>, and a payload (the data).</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: v=
ar(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px=
; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);"=
>wal_write_record()</code>: Appends this metadata to the log file in memory=
.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: v=
ar(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px=
; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);"=
>wal_flush()</code>: Forces the OS to physically write the log buffer to th=
e hard drive (<code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); b=
order: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px=
; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">fflush</code>). T=
his is what happens when you type <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background:=
 var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4=
px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary)=
;">COMMIT</code>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;"><strong style=3D"font-=
weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"bac=
