primary);">recovery.h</code> and <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: =
var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4p=
x; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);=
">recovery.c</code> (Crash Recovery)</strong></p>
<ul style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-d=
irection: column; gap: 3px;">
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;"><code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: v=
ar(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px=
; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);"=
>recover_database()</code>: When <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: =
var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4p=
x; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);=
">minidb</code> starts up, it runs this function first.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">It reads the binary log file from start to =
finish.</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 1.6;">For every <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"bac=
kground: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-r=
adius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-=
primary);">INSERT</code> or <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(-=
-bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; pa=
dding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">UPD=
ATE</code> it finds, it calls your <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background=
: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: =
4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary=
);">fetch_page()</code> Buffer Pool function to grab the page, reapplies th=
e data, and marks the page <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--=
