 key or full page)</code></p>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">Why it failed:</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">When you typed <code c=
lass=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(=
--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--te=
xt-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">insert into users ( name , age ) value=
s ( 'nan' , 23 )</code>, my code converted the first value (<code class=3D"=
mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border=
-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); =
color: var(--text-primary);">'nan'</code>) into an integer to use as the B-=
Tree key.
Because <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border:=
 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font=
-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">'nan'</code> is a strin=
g and not a number, <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-rais=
ed); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1=
px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">atoi("nan")=
</code> evaluates to <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-rai=
sed); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: =
1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">0</code>.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">If you try to insert a=
nother record with a string as the first column, <code class=3D"mono" style=
=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); b=
order-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(=
--text-primary);">atoi()</code> will again evaluate it as <code class=3D"mo=
no" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-s=
ubtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); co=
lor: var(--text-primary);">0</code>. The B-Tree sees that <code class=3D"mo=
no" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-s=
ubtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); co=
lor: var(--text-primary);">0</code> is already in the page, thinks it's a d=
uplicate key, and rejects the insert!</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-size: var(--text-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0px =
6px;">How to fix it:</h3>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">In our new V2 architec=
ture, the B-Tree expects an integer key. We need to pass the <code class=3D=
"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--borde=
r-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm);=
 color: var(--text-primary);">age</code> column as the key, not the <code c=
lass=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(=
--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--te=
xt-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">name</code> column.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">I just updated <code c=
lass=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(=
--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--te=
xt-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">executor.c</code> to parse the <code c=
lass=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(=
--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--te=
xt-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">table</code> struct, specifically look=
 for the <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border=
: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; fon=
t-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">age</code> column, and=
 safely extract the integer.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 8px; line-height: 1.65;">I also compiled it int=
o a new executable called <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--b=
g-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padd=
ing: 1px 5px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">main2=
.exe</code> to avoid the "Permission denied" error (which happens if your o=
ld <code class=3D"mono" style=3D"background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px =
solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size=
: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-primary);">main.exe</code> is still run=
ning or locked).</p>
